    "description": "A Software Engineer with over 19 years of experience in Software Development including analysis/design, programming, consulting, and architecture.  I’ve supported the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) for over 12 years.  Provided systems engineering and software development support to the FAA which has included: agile development concepts using scrum, continuous delivery, good design patterns, best practices and utilizing testing for unit, integration, UI, developed web services, web service clients, web applications, desktop applications, extracted, parsed, formatted, and loaded aeronautical data; built and maintained databases; and served as one of two of primary Geographical Information Systems (GIS) programmer/analysts with responsibility for building GIS software applications and tools,  responsible  for preparation of requirement documents, test plans, Web Service Description Documents (WSDDs), and Web Service Requirements Documents (WSRDs); validation of Federal NOTAM System (FNS) event scenario requirements documentation and Aeronautical Information Exchange Model (AIXM) messages; results oriented Systems Programmer. ",
